WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Twelve checks.

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.767
For filtering: each Internet Access policy
links an existing profile and excludes

3
00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:12.681
emergency access; the acceptable-use categories
and threat intelligence are blocked;

4
00:00:12.681 --> 00:00:15.802
every bypass is owned,
approved and unexpired;

5
00:00:15.802 --> 00:00:20.812
QUIC is blocked by the interim path;
and the tenant is inside Learn's limits.

6
00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:26.138
For TLS: more than ninety days left on a
certificate issued for at least six months;

7
00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:29.397
an issuer that isn't an
authentication authority;

8
00:00:29.397 --> 00:00:34.563
never the baseline profile before ring
3; the privacy approval and user notice

9
00:00:34.563 --> 00:00:39.412
recorded; every custom bypass registered;
and failures under one percent.

10
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:43.176
One note: no Graph read for
TLS inspection was verified,

11
00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.650
so its record comes from the portal.
